{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-039", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["improve", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Trina Solar researchers propose new classification of ultraviolet-induced degradation in TOPCon solar cells", "content": "<p>Trina Solar researchers have proposed a new classification distinguishing reversible and irreversible ultraviolet-induced degradation in TOPCon solar cells. The framework aims to improve reliability testing, identify persistent performance losses, and provide more accurate assessments of long-term module performance under real-world conditions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/trina-solar-researchers-propose-new-classification-of-ultraviolet-induced-degradation-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/14/trina-solar-researchers-propose-new-classification-of-ultraviolet-induced-degradation-in-topcon-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
